Concepts LLC, O2 Blast, AM Leonard -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Metro Plastics Technologies, LLC., established in 1975, is a growing plastic injection molding company.", "founded_year": "1975", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='metro-plastics-technologies-llc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='MiDAS Foods International operates from its main campus in Oak Park, Michigan, with a second facility in Birmingham, Alabama. The company has been developing dry blends for commercial kitchens for over 40 years. Leadership includes partners Richard Elias, serving as president, and Gary Freeman, executive vice president of corporate development.

The company manufactures custom dry blends for sauces, seasonings, glazes, gravies, soups, batters, and dessert mixes. Its combined R&D and manufacturing footprint exceeds 150,000 square feet across the two U.S. sites, supplemented by an affiliate plant in Kashipur, India, that ships to more than 20 countries. The culinary team, led by executive chefs Jerry McDonald and Casey Schallert, handles formula development, clean-label systems, and plant-based ingredient platforms.

MiDAS supplies casual dining restaurant chains and food processors nationwide. Restaurant customers use the blends to replace scratch-made sauces and reduce prep time, while manufacturers incorporate them as single-ingredient solutions to cut SKU count, storage costs, and shipping weight. Regional product lines cover North/Midwest flavors such as Michigan baked bean seasoning and beer cheese fondue, and South/Southeast items like Alabama white barbecue sauce and Nashville hot sauce mix.

The company emphasizes that its dry blends lower total cost by minimizing shipping, eliminating refrigeration, and cutting waste. It also promotes custom formulation capabilities that match or exceed scratch culinary standards while improving batch consistency and production throughput.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Dry blend manufacturing", "Food product development", "Culinary research and development", "Custom recipe formulation", "Clean label ingredient systems", "Plant-based ingredient systems", "Manufacturing optimization", "R&D and pilot production", "Large-scale food manufacturing", "Seasoning and sauce blend production", "Dessert mix production", "Batter and breading mix production", "Soup and sauce mix production", "Glaze and gravy mix production", "Rub and seasoning blend production"], "industries": ["Casual dining restaurants", "Food processors", "Food manufacturers", "Restaurant chains", "Food service"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Award-winning dry blends recognized by RCA and Bell Flavorology", "150,000+ sq ft of combined R&D and manufacturing space in the U.S.", "Custom recipe development led by executive chefs and R&D staff", "Dry blends that reduce shipping weight, eliminate refrigeration, and cut waste", "Nationwide distribution to casual dining and food manufacturing customers"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Oak Park, Michigan -> /", "Southeast campus in Birmingham, Alabama -> /", "Over 150,000 sq ft combined R&D & manufacturing space -> /", "Affiliate Dry Blend Foods in Kashipur, India exporting to 20+ countries -> /", "Operating for over 40 years -> /", "Produces dry blends for sauces, seasonings, glazes, gravies, soups, batters, desserts -> /", "Serves casual dining restaurants and food processors/manufacturers -> /about", "Team includes President Richard Elias, EVP Gary Freeman, executive chefs Jerry McDonald and Casey Schallert -> /about",