UPDATE companies SET description='Micro Metals, Inc. was founded in 1972 by Kenny Driscoll in Colorado Springs, Colorado, at an elevation of 6,272 feet. The company remains family-owned and operated by the Driscoll family, who have grown it into a single-source manufacturer of precision metal parts serving customers across the Midwest, West, and South from its Rocky Mountain location.

The 141,000-square-foot facility, backed by 208,000 square feet of secured outside storage, houses three automated laser cutting systems, a high-capacity robotic press brake, robotic and manual welding cells, CNC machining centers (VMC, HMC, VTC), coil punching and rollforming lines, and an automated powder- and liquid-coating division certified for CARC paint. An experienced workforce—machinists average 15 years on the shop floor and the engineering team includes military veterans—supports in-house design, engineering, assembly, and finishing.

Micro Metals serves the telecommunications, U.S. military, energy, climate-control, construction, and secure-storage sectors, supplying local, national, and international clients. The company also produces components for humanitarian building projects on four continents, including orphanages in Venezuela, rehabilitation centers in Eastern Europe, a food-distribution center in Haiti, and a medical center in Africa.

Automated processes and ISO 9001, NADCAP, and CARC certifications enable consistent quality at scale, while the Colorado Springs location offers transportation efficiencies for rapid delivery.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001','NADCAP','CARC (Chemical Agent Resistant Coating)']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Robotic & Manual Press Brakes", "Automated Laser Cutting", "Robotic & Manual Welding", "Automated Powder & Liquid Coating", "Automated Coil Punching & Rollforming", "CNC Machining (VMC, HMC, VTC)", "CNC Punching", "Blanking & Punching", "Assembly & Support", "Engineering", "Surface Finishing", "Waterjet Cutting", "Chemical Agent Resistant Coating (CARC) Paint"], "industries": ["Telecommunications", "U.S. Military", "Energy", "Climate Control", "Construction", "Secure Storage"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["3 automated laser cutting systems", "Robotic press brake", "Waterjet machines", "CNC machining centers (VMC, HMC, VTC)", "Coil punching and rollforming equipment", "Automated powder and liquid coating line", "Robotic and manual welding cells", "CNC punching equipment", "Blanking and punching equipment", "State-of-the-art inspection equipment"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Single-source manufacturing: quote, design, fabricate, assemble, and ship under one roof", "In-house CARC-certified powder and liquid coating", "Three automated laser cutting systems and robotic press brake", "141,000 sq ft facility with 208,000 sq ft outside storage", "Family-owned with experienced workforce (machinists average 15 years)"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1972 -> db, /about-us", "Location Colorado Springs, Colorado -> /about-us", "Family-owned, Driscoll family -> /about-us", "Founder Kenny Driscoll -> /about-us", "Facility 141,000 sq ft + 208,000 sq ft outside storage -> /about-us", "Certifications ISO 9001, NADCAP, CARC -> db, /about-us", "Capabilities list -> /capabilities, /", "Industries: Telecommunications, U.S. Military, Energy, Clim