UPDATE companies SET description='Micro-Precision Technologies, Inc. (MPT) was founded in 1998 in Salem, New Hampshire. The company focuses on thick-film hybrid microelectronics and semiconductor packaging designed for harsh environments.

MPT produces thick-film circuits screened onto ceramic substrates such as alumina, aluminum nitride, and beryllium oxide, offering a robust alternative to traditional FR-4 printed circuit boards. Its capabilities include FR-4 to ceramic substrate conversion, hybrid assembly with both manual and automated surface-mount technology, wire bonding (ball and wedge), die attach with automated dispensing for epoxy, encapsulant, or optical fluid, and semiconductor die repackaging for improved thermal performance or pinout configuration. All assembly work is performed in a Class 10,000 cleanroom, and the company supports new product introduction as well as consigned or full turnkey assembly.

The company serves industrial, military, and medical markets. Its products are used in applications that demand operation under extreme heat, high vibration, downhole mining conditions, deep-sea wells, and space environments, including power semiconductor packaging challenges.

MPT emphasizes the inherent thermal management of ceramic substrates, which dissipate heat more efficiently than epoxy-based FR-4, and maintains certifications including MIL-PRF-38534 Class H qualification since 1998, QML-38534 listing, DSCC certification, AS9100D, ISO 9001:2015, and ITAR registration.', certifications=ARRAY['MIL-PRF-38534 Class H','QML-38534','DSCC certified','AS9100D','ISO 9001:2015','ITAR registered']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Thick-film circuit screening on ceramic substrates", "FR-4 to ceramic substrate conversion", "Hybrid assembly (SMT, wire bonding, die attach)", "Die attach (manual and automated)", "Wire bonding (ball and wedge)", "Semiconductor die repackaging", "Class 10,000 cleanroom assembly", "New Product Introduction (NPI)", "Consigned and full turnkey assembly"], "industries": ["Industrial", "Military", "Medical"], "materials": ["Alumina", "Aluminum Nitride", "Beryllium Oxide", "FR-4"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["MIL-PRF-38534 Class H qualified since 1998", "AS9100D and ISO 9001:2015 certified", "ITAR registered", "Class 10,000 cleanroom assembly", "Thick-film hybrid circuits on ceramic substrates for high-temperature environments"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1998 -> db", "Headquarters in Salem, New Hampshire -> db", "MIL-PRF-38534 Class H qualified since 1998 -> /", "QML-38534 listed -> /", "DSCC certified -> /", "AS9100D certified -> /", "ISO 9001:2015 certified -> /", "ITAR registered -> /", "Class 10,000 cleanroom -> /", "Thick film hybrid circuits on ceramic substrates -> /", "FR-4 to ceramic conversion -> /", "Hybrid assembly (SMT, wire bonding, die attach) -> /", "Die attach and wire bonding (ball and wedge) -> /", "Semiconductor die repackaging -> /", "Industries: Industrial, Military, Medical -> db", "Materials: Alumina, Aluminum Nitride, Beryllium Oxide, FR-4 -> /", "LinkedIn URL -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence"