UPDATE companies SET description='MicroLink Devices was founded in 2000 in Niles, Illinois, a northern suburb of Chicago. The company operates a 30,000-square-foot facility that includes a clean room and device fabrication and test laboratory.

The company designs and manufactures III-V epitaxial materials for wireless devices and high-efficiency, single- and multi-junction GaAs-based solar cells and sheets. Its proprietary epitaxial lift-off (ELO) process removes the solar cell structure from the growth substrate, yielding lightweight, flexible cells while allowing substrate reuse. MicroLink owns metalorganic chemical vapor deposition (MOCVD) tools for high-volume epitaxial growth, along with full fabrication and test capabilities for semiconductor devices and solar cells. It also performs contract research and development, having served as a prime federal contractor on more than thirty programs since 2003.

Its solar cells and sheets are used in unmanned aerial vehicles, spacecraft, and terrestrial solar collectors. The epitaxial materials support cellular phone and wireless device manufacturers. The company has been a prime contractor on over thirty federal programs developing solar cells, transistors, and lasers.

The company emphasizes quality control, with ISO 9001 certification and a policy of verifying customer specifications before production. Its technical staff includes recognized experts in GaAs and InP device growth and processing, supporting customers through development and production. The ELO technology, developed through federal R&D programs, differentiates its solar products by enabling lightweight, flexible cells with reduced cost through substrate reuse.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["III-V epitaxial material design and manufacturing", "Solar cell and solar sheet design and manufacturing", "Epitaxial lift-off (ELO) processing", "Metalorganic chemical vapor deposition (MOCVD)", "Semiconductor device fabrication and test", "Contract research and development", "Engineering services"], "industries": ["Unmanned aerial vehicles (UAVs)", "Spacecraft", "Terrestrial solar collectors", "Cellular and wireless devices", "Federal/defense research and development"], "materials": ["Gallium Arsenide (GaAs)", "Indium Phosphide (InP)", "III-V compound semiconductors"], "equipment": ["Metalorganic chemical vapor deposition (MOCVD) tools", "Clean room facility", "Device fabrication and test laboratory"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Proprietary epitaxial lift-off (ELO) process for lightweight, flexible solar cells", "Substrate reuse capability lowering cell cost", "ISO 9001 certified quality management", "Metalorganic chemical vapor deposition (MOCVD) tools for high-volume epitaxial growth", "Prime federal contractor on 30+ R&D programs since 2003"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2000 -> /about-us", "30,000 sq ft facility in Niles, IL -> /about-us", "ISO 9001 certified -> /about-us", "Proprietary ELO technology -> /about-us", "MOCVD tools for high-volume production -> /about-us", "Prime federal contractor on 30+ programs since 2003 -> /about-us", "Design/manufacture III-V epitaxial materials for wireless devices -> /about-us", "Design/manufacture solar cells/sheets for UAVs, spacecraft, terrestrial collectors -> /about-us", "Clean room and device fabrication/test lab -> /about-us", "Technical staff experts in GaAs/InP -> /about-us", "Contract R&D services -> /about-us", "Solar cells manufactured using ELO technology -> /", "Single- and multi-junction GaAs-based solar cells -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "MicroLink Devices'' core business is the design and manufacture of III-V epitaxial material used in cellular phones and other wireless devices, and the design and manufacture of solar cells and solar sheets for a variety of applications, including unmanned aerial vehicles (UAVs), spacecraft, and terrestrial collectors.", "founded_year": "2000", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='microlink-devices-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Micropulse Incorporated was established in 1988 by Brian Emerick in a 240-square-foot section of his family garage in Columbia City, Indiana. The company has operated from that same community since its founding, with Emerick remaining as CEO and founder.

Since 2003 Micropulse has concentrated exclusively on the orthopedic market, operating four product lines under one roof: orthopedic instruments, orthopedic implants, custom-made cases and trays, and sterile packaging.

The company serves major, mid-tier, small, and start-up orthopedic device manufacturers. Customers include orthopedic companies that rely on Micropulse for supply-chain responsiveness and regulatory compliance.

