UPDATE companies SET description='Microwave Circuits, based in Lynchburg, Virginia, has been delivering high-performance microwave components since 1994. The brand operates under TTE Filters, a company that designs and manufactures RF and microwave filters for critical applications.

The company produces a range of RF and microwave filters, diplexers, triplexers, quadplexers, bias tees, amplitude equalizers, and EMI/RFI filters covering frequencies from DC to 40 GHz. Its manufacturing expertise spans printed circuits, ceramics, lumped components, helical resonators, machined cavities, and waveguides, allowing integration of multiple technologies into a single filtering device. In-house facilities include 20 network analyzer test stations, full CNC machining capability, and vibration and environmental test equipment, supporting a three-phase testing process.

Microwave Circuits serves defense, aerospace, high-reliability commercial, and scientific customers, as well as broader commercial, industrial, and medical sectors. Its components are used in cellular, data acquisition, electronic support, radar, satellite, sonar, telecommunication, telemetry, and wireless systems by OEMs and organizations worldwide.

The company emphasizes innovative approaches to filter challenges, consistent on-time delivery, and quick turnaround enabled by a product stocking system and raw material inventories. It maintains a quality assurance program based on MIL-Q-9858 and MIL-I-45208, with in-house upscreening to MIL-PRF-15733 and MIL-PRF-28861, and is ITAR registered.', certifications=ARRAY['ITAR','MIL-Q-9858','MIL-I-45208','MIL-PRF-15733','MIL-PRF-28861']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["RF/microwave filter design and manufacturing", "Diplexer, triplexer, quadplexer production", "Bias tee manufacturing", "Amplitude equalizer production", "EMI/RFI filter manufacturing", "Printed circuit fabrication", "Ceramic processing", "Lumped component assembly", "Helical resonator machining", "Machined cavity fabrication", "Waveguide fabrication", "Network analyzer testing (20 stations)", "CNC machining", "Vibration testing", "Environmental testing", "Quality assurance per MIL-Q-9858/MIL-I-45208", "Upscreening to MIL-PRF-15733/MIL-PRF-28861"], "industries": ["Defense", "Aerospace", "Commercial", "Industrial", "Medical", "Scientific", "Telecommunications", "Radar", "Satellite", "Sonar", "Electronic support", "Data acquisition", "Cellular"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Network analyzer test stations (20)", "CNC machining centers", "Vibration test systems", "Environmental test chambers"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Innovative filter design approaches for complex RF challenges", "Three-phase testing process for highest quality", "Consistent on-time delivery commitment", "Off-the-shelf availability and quick turnaround via stocked inventory", "ITAR registered with MIL-spec quality assurance and upscreening capabilities"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Lynchburg, Virginia -> db", "Founded in 1994 -> /about", "Manufactures RF/microwave filters from DC to 40 GHz -> /about, /", "Produces diplexers, triplexers, quadplexers, bias tees, amplitude equalizers, EMI/RFI 