UPDATE companies SET description='Mid America Steel Inc is based in Fargo, North Dakota. Founded in 1905 as an agricultural repair shop and foundry, the company has evolved into a modern steel fabrication firm. It is employee-owned, a structure the company says supports its workforce dedication and community involvement.

The company provides custom metal fabrication including structural steel, pressure vessels, tanks, rebar, plate steel, and miscellaneous metals such as aluminum and stainless steel. Its 40-acre facility in northwest Fargo offers over 220,000 square feet of indoor production space. Key equipment includes a Voortman beam line for shotblasting, sawing, drilling, and robotic coping; an oversized 5-axis plasma cutting table; automated rebar fabrication with stirrup bending and double bender equipment; a full-service machine shop; a 16,000-square-foot paint booth; and a 2,000-square-foot sandblast booth. In-house estimating, drafting, and 3D modeling support the shop, which handles rebar projects ranging from 2,000-ton jobs to small residential slabs.

Mid America Steel serves a broad range of industries across North America. Its fabricated steel products have been used in industrial plants, wastewater treatment facilities, sports arenas, government buildings, hospitals, commercial buildings, agricultural facilities, oil and gas structures, schools, churches, and flood control projects.

The company emphasizes strong customer relationships, willingness to tackle complex projects and tight deadlines, and attributes its capabilities to its skilled, employee-owned workforce. It holds certifications from ASME, AISC, AWS, and the Canadian Welding Board, and operates as an ASME stamp holder for pressure vessels and an AISC-certified fabricator with in-house AWS and CWB certified inspectors.', certifications=ARRAY['ASME','AISC','AWS','CWB']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Structural steel fabrication", "Pressure vessel fabrication", "Tank fabrication", "Rebar fabrication", "Plate steel fabrication", "Miscellaneous metals fabrication (aluminum, stainless steel)", "Staircase and railing fabrication", "Automated rebar fabrication (stirrup bending, double bender)", "Full-service machine shop", "Painting and coating", "Sandblasting", "Galvanizing", "Powder coating", "In-house estimating and drafting", "3D modeling (SDS/2)", "Certified welding inspection", "Welding (AISC/ASME certified)", "Shotblasting", "Sawing", "Drilling", "Robotic coping", "Plasma cutting", "Beveling", "Plate cutting"], "industries": ["Industrial plants", "Wastewater treatment plants", "Sports arenas", "Government buildings", "Hospitals", "Commercial buildings", "Agricultural facilities", "Oil & gas structures", "Schools", "Churches", "Flood projects"], "materials": ["Structural Steel", "Plate Steel", "Rebar", "Aluminum", "Stainless Steel"], "equipment": ["Voortman beam line", "Oversized 5-axis plasma cutting table", "Automated rebar fabrication system (stirrup bending, double bender)", "Full-service machine shop", "16,000 sq ft paint booth", "2,000 sq ft sandblast booth", "SDS/2 3D modeling software"], "volume": "Rebar: 2,000+ ton jobs to backyard patio slabs", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Employee-owned workforce", "40-acre, 220,000-sq-ft indoor fabrication facility", "Voortman beam line for shotblasting, sawing, drilling, and robotic coping", "Automated rebar fabr