UPDATE companies SET description='Milco Industries, a family-owned textile manufacturer, has operated from Bloomsburg, Pennsylvania since its founding in 1922. Now in its second century, the company is led by President and CFO Sabrina Hunsinger, with Travis Carr heading sales and Justin Wark serving as general manager. The business began as a warp knit fabric producer and has remained in the same central Pennsylvania location for over 100 years.

The company runs a fully vertical operation at its Bloomsburg facility, handling knitting, dyeing, and finishing under one roof. Its forming capabilities cover tricot, raschel, and circular knitting, complemented by pad dyeing, brushing, unbroken-loop (UBL) finishing, calendering, and a range of specialty finishes such as anti-microbial, UV-resistant, fire-retardant, and moisture-management treatments. The plant also offers color matching, fabric analysis, direct-to-fabric and heat-transfer printing, and in-house quality control with lab testing on every production batch.

Milco serves a broad spectrum of markets with products that include netting, mesh, suede, satin, jersey, stretch spandex, hook-compatible loop fabrics, and print substrates. Customers can source custom-developed fabrics, commission dyeing and finishing services, or draw from a stock program. The company''s ANSI-compliant and performance-oriented textiles find use in applications requiring durability, safety, and specific functional properties.

Milco emphasizes its Made-in-USA production, ISO 9001:2015 certified quality system, and a shipping process designed to exceed customer requirements. The firm''s longevity and vertical integration allow it to control quality from yarn to finished fabric, a differentiator it highlights alongside its commitment to veteran employment.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','RoHS']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Tricot knitting", "Raschel knitting", "Circular knitting", "Pad dyeing", "Color matching", "Brushing", "UBL (unbroken loop) finishing", "Calendering", "Anti-microbial finishing", "UV resistant finishing", "Anti-abrasion finishing", "Fire retardant finishing", "Wicking finishing", "Hydrophilic finishing", "Moisture management finishing", "Durable water repellent finishing", "Direct-to-fabric printing", "Heat transfer printing", "Fabric analysis", "Quality control and lab testing", "Commission dyeing and finishing", "Custom fabric development", "Stock fabric program", "ANSI compliance testing"], "industries": [], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Vertical integration: knitting, dyeing, and finishing in a single Bloomsburg facility", "ISO 9001:2015 certified quality management system", "Over 100 years of continuous operation since 1922", "Made-in-USA manufacturing with a focus on veteran employment", "Exceptional shipping and packaging process tailored to customer requirements"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1922 -> db", "Family-owned -> db", "Headquarters Bloomsburg, PA -> db", "ISO 9001:2015 certified -> /", "Vertical fabric manufacturer (knit, dye, finish) -> /about", "Tricot, raschel, circular knitting -> /", "Pad dyeing -> /", "Brushing, UBL finishing, calendering -> /", "Finishing capabilities (anti-microbial, UV resistant, fire retardant, etc.) -> /", "Quality control and lab testing -> /", "Products: netting, mesh, suede, satin, jersey, stretch spandex, loop fabrics, print substrates -> /", "Commission dyeing and finishing, custom fabric solutions, stock program -> /services", "Management: Sabrina Hunsinger (President/CFO), Travis Carr (sales), Justin Wark (General manager) -> /about", "Made in USA -> /", "Exceptional shipping process -> /", "100 years experience -> /", "RoHS compliance -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Milco is a vertical fabric manufacturer located in central PA with the ability to knit, dye, and finish a wide variety of fabrics.", "founded_year": "1922", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='milco-industries' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Mile High Metal Fab operates from Arvada, Colorado, serving the Denver metropolitan area with custom metal and wood fabrication. The company focuses on blending structural metalwork with carpentry to create outdoor and interior structures.

The shop provides custom metal fabrication and carpentry services, producing a range of products that include fences, gates, railings, decks, pergolas, patio covers, fire pits, outdoor kitchens, and window well covers. Projects combine metal and wood elements, with the team handling design, fabrication, and installation for both residential and commercial clients.

The company works with homeowners and businesses across the Denver Metro region. Its projects appear in residential backyards, commercial properties, and public spaces, delivering functional and aesthetic structures such as ornamental railings, security fencing, and outdoor living areas.

Mile High Metal Fab emphasizes a blend of craftsmanship and design excellence, aiming to deliver strength, style, and timeless appeal. The firm highlights its ability to merge the durability of metal with the warmth of wood, tailoring each build to the client’s vision while ensuring resilience against Colorado’s climate.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom metal fabrication", "Carpentry", "Custom design", "Welding", "Woodworking", "Fence fabrication", "Gate fabrication", "Railing fabrication", "Deck construction", "Pergola construction", "Patio cover construction", "Fire pit fabrication", "Outdoor kitchen construction", "Window well cover fabrication", "Interior railing fabrication", "Remodeling"], "industries": ["Residential construction", "Commercial construction", "Outdoor living", "Architectural metalwork"], "materials": ["Metal", "Wood"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Combines metal and wood in custom fabrication", "Tailors each project to client vision", "Builds for Colorado climate durability", "Serves both residential and commercial clients", "Offers custom design and fabrication from concept to installation"], "facts_used": ["Location: Arvada, Colorado -> db", "Services: custom metal fabrication and carpentry -> /", "Products: fences, gates, railings, decks, pergolas, patio covers, fire pits, outdoor kitchens, window well covers -> /", "Customer types: homeowners and businesses -> /", "Differentiators: blend of metal and wood, tailored to vision, built for Colorado climate -> /", "Capabilities: Custom Design & Fabrication -> db", "Service details: outdoor living spaces, fences & gates, custom fabrication & specialty builds -> /services"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We design and build fences, gates, and railings, as well as decks, pergolas, patio covers, fire pits, outdoor kitchens, and more", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='mile-high-metal-fab' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Miller Metal Fabrication, based in Bridgeville, Delaware, has been providing precision fabrication services across the Mid-Atlantic region for over 25 years. The company, led by President Martin W. Miller, serves customers from Baltimore to Philadelphia and works with international corporations, local businesses, and entrepreneurs alike.

The shop offers a range of in-house capabilities including CNC laser cutting (with two Trumpf TruLaser 5030 fiber lasers and a TruLaser 5040), tube laser cutting, CNC punching, CNC forming, CNC machining, and MIG/TIG and robotic welding. It also provides 3D CAD design and CAD conversion services, allowing it to turn sketches into workable parts. The facility runs a Bliss C-250 stamping press and uses lean manufacturing and just-in-time concepts to handle both small jobs and large production runs.

Miller Metal works primarily with carbon steel, stainless steel, aluminum, and galvanized materials. Its customer base spans the Mid-Atlantic corridor, including the Baltimore, Washington, and Philadelphia metro areas, and includes international corporations, small local businesses, and entrepreneurs developing new products.

The company emphasizes lean processes and short lead times, often delivering in a few days or even one day. President Miller''s philosophy — “You pay for the product, not the name” — reflects a focus on value and competitive pricing. Miller Metal holds ISO 9001 certification and has earned a BBB A+ rating and a Workplace Health and Safety Incentive Program Award.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["CNC laser cutting", "Tube laser cutting", "CNC punching", "CNC forming", "CNC machining", "CNC HD plasma cutting", "MIG welding", "TIG welding", "Robotic welding", "3D CAD design", "CAD conversion", "Stamping", "Sheet metal fabrication", "Precision fabrication"], "industries": [], "materials": ["Carbon steel", "Stainless steel", "Aluminum", "Galvanized steel"], "equipment": ["Trumpf TruLaser 5030 Fiber Laser", "Trumpf TruLaser 5040 Fiber Laser", "Bliss C-250 Stamping Press"], "volume": "Small jobs to large production runs", "lead_time": "A few days or even one day", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Lean manufacturing and just-in-time concepts enabling lead times of a few days or one day", "In-house robotic welding alongside MIG/TIG welding", "State-of-the-art tube laser with swiveling head for complex weldment miters", "Trumpf fiber laser cutting systems (5030 and 5040 models)", "Turnkey fabrication from CAD through machining and welding"], "facts_used": ["Location: Bridgeville, Delaware -> db, /about-us", "Operating for over 25 years -> /about-us", "President Martin W. Miller -> /about-us", "Services Mid-Atlantic region including Baltimore, Washington, Philadelphia -> /about-us", "Serves international corporations, small local businesses, entrepreneurs -> /about-us", "Uses lean manufacturing and just-in-time concepts -> /about-us", "Lead time a few days or even one day -> /about-us", "Quote ''You pay for the product, not the name'' -> /about-us", "ISO 9001 certification -> /about-us, db", "BBB A+ rating as of 1/20/2016 -> /about-us", "Workplace Health and Safety Incentive Program Award -> /about-us", "2012 Entrepreneurial Success Award Winner Martin W. Miller -> /about-us", "Equipment: 2 Trumpf TruLaser 5030 Fiber Lasers, Trumpf TruLaser 5040 Fiber Laser -> /", "Equipment: Bliss C-250 Stamping Press -> db", "Capabilities: CNC laser cutting, tube laser cutting, CNC punching, CNC forming, CNC machining, CNC HD plasma cutting, MIG/TIG welding, robotic welding, 3D CAD, CAD conversion -> /, /about-us", "Materials: carbon steel, stainless, aluminum, galvanized -> /, /about-us", "Turnkey products -> /about-us", "Flexible quantities, logistical chain management -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "MillerMetal offers in-house MIG and TIG welding for carbon steel, stainless, aluminum and galvanized applications.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='miller-metal-fabrication' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Milwaukee Electronics was founded in 1954 in Milwaukee, Wisconsin, as a design and manufacturing center integrating electronics into heavy machinery for the mining industry. In 1988 it completed its first microprocessor design for the generator industry, and in 1999 established a nearshore facility in Tecate, Mexico, chosen for its proximity to San Diego.

The company provides printed circuit board assembly, electronic design, and full manufacturing services, operating a 23,000-square-foot facility in Tecate alongside a purchasing office in Singapore and a technology center in India. Its capabilities span prototype through high-mix, mid-to-high-volume production, supported by lean manufacturing practices adopted in 2001 and a patented cut-tape machine assembly process for e-commerce prototyping launched in 2003.

Milwaukee Electronics serves the generator, mining, and heavy-machinery sectors, with certifications that also align it to aerospace (AS9100) and medical device (ISO 13485) markets. Customers include original equipment manufacturers requiring supply-chain navigation amid material constraints and tariff shifts.

The firm differentiates itself through its nearshore Tecate operation—one hour from San Diego—and its early creation of an e-commerce PCB assembly service (Screaming Circuits) for rapid prototyping. A recent poll cited 96% customer confidence in its handling of material constraints.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO9001','AS9100','ISO13485']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["PCB assembly", "Electronic design", "Electronic manufacturing", "Lean manufacturing", "Prototyping", "High-mix mid-to-high volume production", "Supply chain management", "Nearshore manufacturing", "E-commerce PCB assembly", "Microprocessor design"], "industries": ["Generator industry", "Mining industry", "Heavy machinery"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "High mix, mid-to-high volume", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["First e-commerce PCB assembly service (Screaming Circuits) launched in 2003", "Nearshore manufacturing in Tecate, Mexico, one hour from San Diego", "Lean manufacturing implemented since 2001 to reduce lead times", "Global supply chain with Asia purchasing office in Singapore", "96% customer confidence in navigating material constraints (per recent poll)"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1954 in Milwaukee, Wisconsin -> db and page ''/''", "Began integrating electronics into heavy machinery for mining industry -> page ''/''", "Completed first microprocessor design for generator industry in 1988 -> page ''/''", "Established Tecate, Mexico facility in 1999 -> page ''/''", "Implemented lean manufacturing in 2001 -> page ''/''", "Launched first e-commerce PCB assembly service (Screaming Circuits) in 2003 -> page ''/''", "Opened Asia purchasing office in Singapore in 2011 -> page ''/''", "Expanded Tecate facility by 23,000 sq ft in 2019 -> page ''/''", "Certifications: ISO9001, AS9100, ISO13485 -> db", "High mix/mid-to-high volume manufacturing -> page ''/''", "96% customer confidence in handling material constraints -> page ''/''", "Nearshore manufacturing one hour from San Diego -> page ''/''"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Milwaukee Electronics began by integrating electronics into heavy machinery", "founded_year": "1954", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='milwaukee-electronics' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Minnesofa Furniture was founded in May 2022 by Max Bjorklund and Luke Schultz in Minnesota. The business began in a garage where the pair refurbished used furniture, turning a passion for furniture and entrepreneurship into a vision for a retail operation. Within a year they opened their first store in Moorhead and have since added a second location in Excelsior.

The company operates as a furniture retailer, offering sectionals, sofas, chairs, tables, bedroom sets, mattresses, outdoor pieces, and reclining furniture. Inventory comes through a direct partnership with Ashley Furniture and through the refurbishment of used items, which are sold as like-new condition. Minnesofa also provides a white‑glove delivery service that covers in‑home delivery, assembly, and trash removal across the Twin Cities metro area.

The founders started Minnesofa to combine their interest in furniture with a hands‑on business model. They highlight speed—most items can be delivered within a week—and the personal attention that comes from a locally owned, owner‑operated shop as key differentiators.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Furniture retail", "White glove delivery", "In-home furniture setup", "Trash removal", "Furniture refurbishment", "Furniture sourcing (new and used)"], "industries": [], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "Within a week for most products", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Delivery within a week for most products", "White glove delivery including in-home setup and trash removal", "Locally owned and operated with direct owner interaction", "Direct partnership with Ashley Furniture for new inventory", "Refurbishment of used furniture for like-new offerings"], "facts_used": ["Founded May 2022 by Max Bjorklund and Luke Schultz -> /", "Started refurbishing used furniture in a garage -> /", "Locations in Moorhead and Excelsior, Minnesota -> /", "Direct partnership with Ashley Furniture -> /", "White glove delivery with in-home setup and trash removal -> /", "Delivery within a week for most products -> /", "Locally owned and operated -> /", "Product categories: sectionals, sofas, chairs, tables, bedroom, mattresses, outdoor, reclining -> /"], "company_type": "Retailer", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Minnesofa currently has a location in Moorhead MN and just launched their new store in Excelsior MN!", "founded_year": "2022", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='minnesofa-furniture' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Minnesota Medical Technologies is headquartered in Stewartville, Minnesota, just outside Rochester, the state''s "Med City." The company was founded by Philip J. Conway, Sarah L. Grinde, and Lonnie M. Boe, veterans of the medical device industry who previously built Arcon Corp. (1979), Rochester Medical Corp. (1988), and BCG Technologies (2013). Their collective experience spans more than three decades of silicone technology and continence care innovation.

The company develops, manufactures, and sells continence care products, with its flagship device StaySure® designed to prevent accidental bowel leakage rather than merely contain or absorb it. The team designs and builds its own highly specialized, high-volume production systems to support silicone-based manufacturing. StaySure® was developed in collaboration with gastroenterologists and targets a condition more prevalent than asthma.

Minnesota Medical Technologies serves the global medical device market, focusing on patients, physicians, and healthcare providers managing fecal incontinence. Its products address a patient population that often avoids seeking care due to embarrassment, offering a discreet solution intended to restore confidence and daily freedom.

The founders started the company because they believed existing fecal incontinence products were inadequate—failing to prevent leakage, control odor, or provide ease of use. Their mission is to deliver continence care products of unmatched performance, comfort, and quality, grounded in a genuine understanding of the daily challenges patients face.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Medical device development", "Silicone technology manufacturing", "Product design and development", "High-volume production system design and building", "Quality system design and implementation", "FDA regulatory affairs (Class I, II, III medical devices)", "Research and development", "Global product deployment", "Continence care product innovation"], "industries": ["Medical devices", "Continence care", "Fecal incontinence management", "Healthcare"], "materials": ["Silicone"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Prevents accidental leakage rather than containing or absorbing it", "Developed with leading gastroenterologists", "Designs and builds proprietary high-volume production systems", "Over 30 years of silicone technology experience", "Products have improved millions of lives globally"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Stewartville, MN -> db", "Founders: Philip J. Conway, Sarah L. Grinde, Lonnie M. Boe -> /about-us", "Previous companies: Arcon Corp (1979), Rochester Medical Corp (1988), BCG Technologies (2013) -> /about-us", "30+ years silicone technology experience -> /about-us", "Mission: develop, make, sell continence care products -> /about-us, /", "Flagship product StaySure\u00ae prevents accidental leakage -> /, /about-us", "Developed with gastroenterologists -> /", "Designs/builds own high-volume production systems -> /about-us", "Serves global market for fecal incontinence -> /, /about-us", "Team includes CEO David A Jones, VP Quality Robert Anglin (FDA Class I-III experience) -> /about-us"], "company_type"