ring -> /capabilities", "Provides manufacturing coordination across partners -> /capabilities", "Produces technical binders for cable assembly designers (QSFP-DD, CABLINE-CA II, CABLINE-VS II) -> /capabilities", "Emphasizes quality discipline with inspection expectations, traceability, continual improvement -> /quality", "Developing GFx\u2122 data transport-physics architecture -> /", "Engineering-led company with manufacturing depth -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Mitas Electronics combines miniature high-speed interconnect experience, precision manufacturing discipline, and future-facing transport architecture work to support more predictable physical data movement as systems scale.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='mitas-electronics' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Mitchell Furniture Systems traces its roots to Milwaukee, Wisconsin, where William Mitchell founded the company in 1896 to produce dairy farming equipment such as automatic stalls and stanchions. The business expanded into steel products for parks and playgrounds before pivoting in the 1940s to folding leg tables, choral risers, and wall-mounted table and bench systems for cafeterias. Today the company operates manufacturing plants in Fredonia and Milwaukee, maintaining a “Made in America” commitment with seasoned metal fabricators and assemblers using both time-honored techniques and robotic welding.

The product line centers on wall-mounted table and bench systems (NPX and ST series), mobile tables with integrated seating (PorTables), fold-and-roll tables (Fold-N-Roll), convertible 3-in-1 ConverTables, adjustable-height folding tables (Saturna and Fold-O-Leg), and risers for stages and seating. The company also offers a table-top replacement service for both its own and competitors’ tables.

Historical markets encompassed dairy farming and municipal park systems. The company cites installations in cafeterias, fellowship halls, classrooms, lecture halls, and theaters as typical applications.

