UPDATE companies SET description='Monterey Mills operates from Janesville, Wisconsin. The company traces its current ownership to February 1995, when Dan Sinykin purchased the former Roller Fabrics after a seven-month unpaid trial period. Sinykin, a Drake University graduate, had previously built a 14-store retail tailor chain and spent six years in sales and marketing at Procter & Gamble. He consolidated multiple manufacturing facilities and expanded the business into automotive, equestrian, apparel, hospital, and pet-product markets.

The mill specializes in sliver knitting (also called high-pile knitting), a labor-intensive process that locks individual acrylic fibers into a lightweight knit backing to create fabrics that are warmer than fleece yet machine washable. An in-house research and development team controls fiber and yarn selection, pile height, density, tensile strength, width, color, and stitch count, enabling custom performance fabrics for diverse applications. The company produces rolled fabrics, paint-roller fabrics, and finished goods for medical, pet, blanket, and bedding lines, all marketed as Made in USA.

Customers span medical and pet-product manufacturers, blanket and bedding brands, automotive and equestrian suppliers, apparel makers, and hospital procurement. The technical team works directly with clients to develop fabrics that meet specific performance requirements, from odor and mildew resistance to colorfastness.

Monterey Mills positions itself as one of the few remaining practitioners of sliver knitting, a craft many competitors abandoned due to its complexity. The company emphasizes sustainability, sourcing recycled raw materials, repurposing all production waste, and treating and reusing wastewater. Continuous improvement in processes and employee skills is cited as the foundation for its quality reputation.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Sliver knitting", "High-pile knitting", "Fiber selection", "Yarn selection", "Pile height control", "Density control", "Tensile strength control", "Width control", "Color control", "Stitch count control", "In-house research and development", "Quality control", "Waste repurposing", "Wastewater treatment and reuse"], "industries": ["Medical", "Pet products", "Blankets & bedding", "Automotive", "Equestrian", "Apparel", "Hospital"], "materials": ["Acrylic fibers", "Recycled raw materials"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["One of the few remaining U.S. manufacturers using sliver-knitting technology", "In-house R&D team controlling fiber, yarn, pile height, density, tensile strength, width, color, and stitch count", "Sustainability program: recycled raw materials, zero-waste production, wastewater treatment and reuse", "All products made in the USA", "Continuous improvement quality system targeting premier sliver-knitter status"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: Janesville, Wisconsin -> db", "Founded/purchased in February 1995 by Dan Sinykin -> /", "Sliver knitting (high-pile knitting) process -> /", "Industries served: medical, pet, blankets, bedding, automotive, equestrian, apparel, hospital -> /", "In-house research and development team controlling fiber, yarn, pile height, density, tensile strength, width, color, stitch count -> /", "Sustainability practices: recycled raw materials, waste repurposing, wastewater treatment and reuse -> /", "Quality control commitment: continuous improvement, premier sliver knitter -> /", "Made in USA products -> /", "Dan Sinykin background: retail tailor chain, Procter & Gamble, Drake University -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Monterey Mills is one of only a few manufacturers remaining that uses this superior technique of producing fabric", "founded_year": "1995", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='monterey-mills' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Montrose Molders operates from Piscataway, New Jersey, where it was founded in 1966 by William Bruce Wilson. The company began as a 22-person tool shop producing tight-tolerance molds for the plastics industry and added its first injection molding press in 1972. Today it remains a family-owned business led by the Wilson family, now in its fourth generation of plastics manufacturing.

The firm runs a vertically integrated operation that covers part design, tooling, molding, extrusion, assembly, and packaging. Its molding department comprises 51 presses ranging from 40 to 1,000 tons of clamp force, supported by two extrusion lines with co-extrusion capability. An on-site tool room builds aluminum and steel production molds, while a 25,000-square-foot assembly area can run five lines simultaneously. Mold-flow simulation uses SolidWorks Plastics software, and industrial design services help translate concepts into 3D models.

Montrose serves customers in retail, battery, automotive, lighting, safety, aerospace, electronics, medical devices, and consumer goods. The company positions itself as a contract plastics manufacturer for original equipment manufacturers and brand owners seeking a single-source partner from prototype through full-scale production.

Management emphasizes a one-stop-shop model intended to shorten lead times, reduce costs, and deliver consistent quality. Each program is assigned a dedicated project manager, and engineering resources span industrial design to tooling validation. The family legacy is cited as a driver of long-term customer relationships and continuous investment in equipment and process control.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom injection molding (40\u20131,000 ton)", "Extrusion with co-extrusion", "Tool and die production (aluminum and steel molds)", "Assembly and packaging (5 lines)", "Mold flow simulation (SolidWorks Plastics)", "Industrial design and engineering", "Part decoration", "Project management", "Tooling engineering"], "industries": ["Retail", "Battery", "Automotive", "Lighting", "Safety", "Aerospace", "Electronics", "Medical devices", "Consumer goods"], "materials": ["Engineering-grade plastics", "Commodity plastics", "Aluminum (for tooling)", "Steel (for tooling)"], "equipment": ["Injection molding presses (40\u20131,000 ton)", "Extrusion lines with co-extrusion", "SolidWorks Plastics Simulation software", "On-site tool room equipment"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Vertically integrated: part design through finished assembly in-house", "51 injection molding presses (40\u20131,000 ton clamp force)", "On-site tool room producing aluminum and steel molds", "25,000 sq ft assembly area with five simultaneous lines", "ISO 9001:2015 certified with dedicated project managers"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1966 -> db, /about", "Headquarters Piscataway, New Jersey -> db", "ISO 9001:2015 certified -> /, /about", "51 injection molding machines 40-1000 tons -> /, /services", "Two extrusion lines with co-extrusion -> /, /services", "On-site tooling shop for aluminum and steel molds -> /about, /services", "25,000 sq ft assembly space, 5 lines -> /, /services", "Family-owned, Wilson family, four generat