UPDATE companies SET description='Mountaineer Fabricators Inc was founded in 1923 as a family-owned fabrication business. In 2004, the company was acquired and moved into a newly constructed facility in Nitro, West Virginia, where it operates today.

The company designs and manufactures ASME-code pressure vessels, pre-fabricated piping assemblies, and modular skidded process units. Its in-house shop provides plate rolling, engine lathe turning, horizontal and vertical boring, CNC milling and drilling, surface grinding, and a full suite of pressure testing including hydrostatic, pneumatic, helium leak detection, and nitrogen sensitive leak methods. Welders are qualified to ASME Section IX and API-1104, and the engineering department performs ASME Section VIII Division 1 design calculations using Compress software alongside AutoCAD drafting. The facility handles piping diameters from 1/4 inch to 120 inches and maintains ASME U, R, S, and NB stamps for fabrication and repair.

Mountaineer Fabricators serves the oil and gas, power generation, chemical processing, and natural gas industries, as well as air separation, steam piping, oxygen and nitrogen production, heat exchanger, glass wool, data center, food processing, and Kevlar-related sectors. Its prefabricated piping assemblies, launchers and receivers, and valve settings are used to reduce field construction costs for customers in those markets.

It emphasizes the combination of modern equipment and a tenured, cross-trained team to achieve extreme precision across diverse industries.', certifications=ARRAY['ASME U Stamp','ASME R Stamp','ASME S Stamp','NB Stamp','ASME Section IX','API-1104','ASME Section VIII Division 1']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Pressure vessel fabrication (ASME U, R, S stamps)", "Pressure vessel repair (NB stamp)", "Pre-fabricated piping assemblies (1/4\" to 120\")", "Skidded process unit fabrication", "Launcher and receiver fabrication", "Process tower fabrication", "Oil and gas separator fabrication", "Tray tower fabrication", "Direct and indirect fired heater fabrication", "Pulsation bottle and drip tank fabrication", "Line heater fabrication", "High pressure piping header fabrication", "Heat exchanger and cooler fabrication", "Storage tank fabrication", "Meter run fabrication", "Plate rolling", "Engine lathe turning", "Horizontal and vertical boring mill machining", "CNC milling and drilling", "Surface grinding", "Pressure testing (hydrostatic, pneumatic, helium leak detection, nitrogen sensitive leak)", "Machine shop fabrication", "Jacketed piping fabrication", "On-site weld, mechanical, and industrial engineering services"], "industries": ["Oil/Gas Industry", "Air Separation Industry", "Steam Piping Industry", "Oxygen & Nitrogen Industry", "ASME Code Vessels Industry", "Heat Exchangers Industry", "Glass Wool Industry", "Data Centers Industry", "Food Industry", "Kevlar Industry", "Power Generation Industry", "Chemical Processing Industry"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Engine lathes", "Horizontal boring mills", "Vertical boring mills", "CNC milling and drilling machines", "Surface grinders", "Plate rolling machines"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["ASME U, R, S, and NB stamps for pressure vessel fabrication and repair", "Welders certified to ASME Section IX and API-1104", "In-house engineering with Compress and AutoCAD for ASME Section VII