UPDATE companies SET description='NOLA Steele Fabrication and Erection LLC was founded in 2014 by Karen L. Williams in Harvey, Louisiana. Williams brought more than two decades of construction industry experience, having risen from office manager to vice president before launching her own firm. The company is certified as a woman-owned, service-disabled veteran-owned small business (SDVOSB), and also holds 8(a), DBE, MBE, WBE, and EDWOSB designations. Her husband, Travis Williams, a service-connected disabled veteran with 15 years in the U.S. Army, serves as vice president and estimator.

The company provides design, steel fabrication, structural steel erection, repair welding, ornamental iron, limited steel demolition, and miscellaneous steel work such as handrails, guardrails, balconies, and stair stringers. It also supplies steel products and furnishes skilled labor including welders, fitters, riggers, tackers, ironworkers, painters, and sandblasters. NOLA Steele operates with a team of about 35 trained professionals and has completed more than 500 projects since inception.

Clients include government agencies such as the U.S. Army Corps of Engineers and the Louis Armstrong New Orleans International Airport, as well as municipalities, nonprofit organizations, and commercial contractors throughout Southeast Louisiana.

Williams established the firm with a mission of superior quality, craftsmanship, and customer satisfaction, emphasizing a thorough quality control program and a vision to train and certify new welders. The company stresses that it is fully licensed, insured, and bonded, and aims to deliver projects on time and within budget.', certifications=ARRAY['SBA 8(a) Certified','Economically Disadvantaged Women-Owned Small Business (EDWOSB) Certified','Disadvantaged Business Enterprise (DBE) Certified','Minority Business Enterprise (MBE) Certified','Woman-Owned Business Enterprise (WBE) Certified','Service Disabled Veteran-Owned Small Business (SDVOSB) Certified']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Steel fabrication", "Structural steel erection", "Repair welding", "Ornamental ironwork", "Limited steel demolition", "Miscellaneous steel fabrication (handrails, guardrails, balconies)", "Stair stringer fabrication and installation", "Steel supply", "Skilled labor provision (welders, fitters, riggers, tackers, ironworkers, painters, sandblasters)", "Design services"], "industries": ["Construction", "Government (federal, state, local)", "Aviation", "Municipalities", "Nonprofit organizations", "Commercial construction"], "materials": ["Steel", "Structural steel"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Over 20 years of industry experience", "More than 500 completed projects", "35 trained professionals on staff", "Licensed, insured, and bonded", "Quality control program integrated into every project"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2014 by Karen L. Williams in Harvey, Louisiana -> /about", "Woman-owned, SDVOSB, 8(a), DBE, MBE, WBE, EDWOSB certifications -> /about", "Travis Williams is service-disabled veteran, VP/Estimator -> /about", "Services: steel fabrication, erection, repair welding, ornamental iron, limited demolition, miscellaneous steel, stair stringers, steel supply, skilled labor -> /services", "35 trained professionals, >500 project